  "scope": "Nine existing E2E consumers plus a new catalogue fixture, global setup and the standalone ordinary database bootstrap. No production step/history/schema or CLI implementation changed.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Dev/QA are explicit fixture definitions with real project bindings, not production defaults.",
    "Custom recipes and rendering fixtures create actual projects and bind the chosen steps before package birth. Rendering creates through validated public API shapes, selects the returned package ID in the real picker and unmounts the observer before batched writes. Existing UI create/rename-arm coverage remains in create-work-package callers.",
    "Package responses keep compatible optional code/unit/allowancePercent fields. Only the current values request uses integer allowanceBps.",
    "Picker selection uses a CSS-escaped observed package ID within the actual listbox; matching display names confer no authority.",
    "The desktop boundary test now measures the existing h-9 allowance input36px, replacing the removed32px add-step button.",
    "Private empty-fixture migration/report/backup/application is not operator session or barrier admission. The ordinary public migrator still refuses pending117. Node assertion functions run under Bun; no Node or shell script was added."
  ],
